From 8714ab433b22c060ede2917cd1a4d8a2a06ff53c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes <johannes.hirche@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:32:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Add a libtiff based TIFF image plugin to the CLI

Without Qt, which the Linux CLI doesn't use, TIFF files could not be
loaded at all, although TIF/TIFF are listed as supported inputs.

The plugin loads the first image of a TIFF file. Gray, gray+alpha, RGB
and RGBA images with 8/16-bit integer or 16/32-bit float samples keep
their precision and straight alpha, stripped or tiled, contiguous or
planar, with any compression and predictor libtiff was built with.
Mirrored orientations are applied. Other photometric interpretations
(palette, bilevel, YCbCr, CMYK, ...) are loaded as 8-bit RGBA through
libtiff's RGBA interface.

Built when OPTION_BUILD_TIFF is on (default on Linux) and libtiff is found.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
